DOMAIN determination rule:
  - A CL / DT / HWD line has exactly ONE target, so it is ALWAYS single-domain:
    CTRL and DATA never share such a line.
  - The domain follows the TARGET (the LHS being written / declared), NOT the RHS.
    For  a <<= b  (or  a = b ):  kind = DT (plain move) or CL (RHS computes);
    DOMAIN = domain of  a  (look  a  up in the list), regardless of  b . E.g.
    busy <<= b -> CTRL_DT ; pc <<= b -> DATA_DT ; comPtr <<= comPtr+1 -> CTRL_CL.
    (The RHS identifiers are counted on the lines that PRODUCE them.) If a target
    is not yet in the list, classify it by role and ADD it to the list.
  - Control-flow constructs with no data subject (clocked-process wrapper,
    if(reset)/stall/kill guards, FSM next-state, HDB flow blocks) are CONTROL by
    nature (kind = CL, so CTRL_CL).
  - HC domain = per-port. The ONLY line carrying both CTRL and DATA is a single
    inseparable HC bundle token -> split CTRL_HC + DATA_HC (0.5 each).
  - MD, PARAM, HLH have NO domain.


=====================================================================
THE KIND AXIS -- what does the line DO?
=====================================================================
---------------------------------------------------------------------
MD -- Module / struct declaration                        (domain-less)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     declaring or instantiating a MODULE or STRUCT (any composite
           user type), as opposed to a hardware PRIMITIVE (that is HWD).
  Covers   type header   struct X{ | struct X: Module{ | module foo
           instance      mMod(...) head | ModuleType inst
                         (RegArch regArch, Rsvs rsvs, ...)
                         Verilog instance head: reorderbuf rob | alu alice
  NOT MD   HWD = a hardware primitive (reg / wire / mem / table / slot)
           HC  = the struct members and the wired args
  Note     line-break the connectivity / members off the head
           -- see MODULE-DECL REFORMATTING.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
HC -- Hardware connectivity                        CTRL_HC / DATA_HC
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     an INTERFACE or CONNECTION: signature / parameter (port) lines,
           ctor-arg and instance connectivity, port-bundle structs and
           their ref members, opr&-returning wrapper signatures, I/O
           tagging, instance port maps.
  Kathryn  (opr& op, opr& srcA, ...)
           struct RenameCmd{ opr& busy; ... }
           {tagMgmt.mpft}              ctor-arg connectivity
           pm, regArch, storeBuf       ctor args
           inline opr& alu <sig>
           asInputGlob / asOutputGlob  I/O tagging
           ctor init-list binds
  Verilog  input / output / inout port decls
           instance port maps          .op(alu_op)
  Domain   busy / valid / kill / sync port   -> CTRL_HC
           data / pc / operand port          -> DATA_HC
           inseparable bundle (PipStage& pm) -> CTRL_HC+DATA_HC (0.5 each)

  SPECIAL CASE -- computed port arg (Verilog)
    A port map whose arg is an EXPRESSION rather than a plain signal:
        logic / arith   .enable(~stall_ID & ~stall_DP)
        ternary mux     .wpc((sel)?a:b)
        concat          {a,b}
        bit-slice       x[hi:lo]   x[b+:w]
    does TWO things on one line -- it connects the port (HC) AND computes
    the value (CL, per the concat/slice/ternary/logic-op = CL rule).
    Tag both, in the SAME domain as the port:   X_HC+X_CL  (0.5 each).
    A plain .port(sig) stays pure HC.
    Symmetric with Kathryn, where such a compute is its own CL line (a zif
    guard, or x = a & b) instead of being hidden inside a port map.

  SPECIAL CASE -- line-broken computed arg
    When the expression spans several physical lines (a long concat
    .entvec({a[..], b[..],   /   c[..], d[..]})), EVERY physical line that
    itself carries a compute portion (a slice or concat token) is
    X_HC+X_CL -- not just the first .name( line. Per the per-physical-line
    rule. 6 such continuation lines: oldest_finder.v, pipeline.v isunt_alu
    concats.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
HWD -- Hardware declaration                      CTRL_HWD / DATA_HWD
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     declare a PERSISTENT hardware PRIMITIVE that holds data or
           named nets: data/control register, named wire/net, memory /
           table / slot storage, SlotMeta field layout.
  Kathryn  mReg / mWire / mExpr
           WireSlot / RegSlot / Table / MemTable / mMem
           SlotMeta
  Verilog  reg / wire / logic
           memory arrays   reg[W:0] mem[0:N]
  ALSO     the CONTROL-STATE register that a CYCLE-ADVANCING HDB header
           instantiates -- the flow-block state / sync / counter register,
           emitted as SR_ST# in the generated Verilog. The header is one
           line doing two jobs, so it scores CTRL_HWD+CTRL_CL (0.5 each);
           this HWD half is that register. Cycle-advancing headers are
           pip / pipe / zync / zyncc / cwhile / while / loop / wait / seq /
           state. A COMBINATIONAL header (zif / zcase / par / pick) creates
           no register and is pure CL.
           Symmetric with RIDECORE, where the same FSM costs two separate
           lines: reg state (CTRL_HWD) + always@(posedge) (CTRL_CL).
  Domain   reg busy        -> CTRL_HWD
           reg [31:0] pc   -> DATA_HWD
  NOT HWD  a struct/class/module, type header OR instance, is MD
           a named constant is PARAM

---------------------------------------------------------------------
CL -- Combinational logic                          CTRL_CL / DATA_CL
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     COMPUTE a value with operators: arith, logic, compare, shift,
           bit-slice, concat, extension, mux/ternary, datapath-select
           conditional.
           ALSO control-flow / sequencing constructs -> CTRL_CL: clocked-
           process wrapper always @(posedge ...), if(reset)/enable/stall/
           flush/kill guards, FSM next-state, update scheduling / priority.
  HDB      an HDB header is PURE CL only when it creates NO state register:
             combinational   zif / zelif / zelse / zcase / ztate-as-decode
                             par / pick            -> CL  (score 1.0)
             cycle-advancing pip / pipe / zync / zyncc / cwhile / while
                             loop / wait / seq / state
                                                   -> CTRL_HWD+CTRL_CL
                             because it ALSO declares the state register
                             -- see HWD. Do not tag these as plain CL.
           A combinational zif gating a control action is CTRL_CL; a
           datapath zif/ztate SELECTING a value is CL by the selected
           value's domain.
  Kathryn  out = srcA + srcB;   shamt = srcB.sl(0,W);  ~(fullBit >> shamt)
           ztate(op){zcase...};  g(...) concat;  .uext / .sext
           SET_ASM_PRI_TO_MANUAL / AUTO
           (pip / zync / cwhile are the HWD+CL case above, not pure CL)
  Verilog  assign y=a+b;  case(op)...;  sel?a:b;  {31'b0,in1==in2}
           always @(posedge clk);  if(reset);  assign stall/kill/valid
  Domain   assign kill=...  -> CTRL_CL
           assign y=a+b     -> DATA_CL

---------------------------------------------------------------------
DT -- Data transfer                                CTRL_DT / DATA_DT
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     MOVE / COPY / ROUTE / STORE a value with NO operators: plain
           signal RHS, struct field, indexed read, register write of a
           signal, array/table/struct element write, RESET-VALUE write.
  Kathryn  busyTemp = busySlot;  busySlot <<= busyTemp
           _table[idx] <<= dpValue
           makeResetEvent / makeColResetEvent / makeDefEvent  (reset value)
  Verilog  assign y=x;  q<=d;  data[finptr]<=stdata;  reset-branch q<=0
  Domain   busy<=issue / busy<=0  -> CTRL_DT
           pc<=npc    / pc<=0     -> DATA_DT
  vs CL    table / array / struct INDEXING is access      -> DT
           bit-SLICE, concat, extend is compute           -> CL

---------------------------------------------------------------------
PARAM -- Parameter / constant                            (domain-less)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     a NAMED CONSTANT / PARAMETER definition: sizes, counts,
           encodings, constant values. Explicitly-constant forms only.
  Kathryn  mVal / mPmVal
           static / const / constexpr numeric consts (incl *_PRIORITY)
           O3_PARAM_STR(name) field / opcode / width identifiers
  Verilog  parameter;  localparam
           `define value macros (`REG_SEL, widths, ops)
  NOT      a plain MUTABLE host var (int idx=-1, reassigned later) is HLH

---------------------------------------------------------------------
HLH -- Host-language helper                              (domain-less)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
  What     host-language CONTROL-STRUCTURE scaffolding -- neither hardware
           nor a constant; the glue the host language needs in order to
           elaborate the hardware.
  Kathryn  for / while host loops;  std:: containers;  templates
           structured bindings auto[a,b]=...;  glue lambdas
           function-like macros (#define str(name));  plain mutable
           int / bool
  Verilog  genvar;  generate/for;  integer i;  initialization loops

=====================================================================
MODULE-DECL REFORMATTING (line-break MD off HC)
=====================================================================
Because MD (the module head) and HC (its wired connectivity) are two kinds, and
one line may carry only one category, line-break every module-instance
declaration so each is its own physical line. Layout-only edit -- valid
C++/Verilog, no semantics:

  // before
  RegArch  regArch {tagMgmt.mpft};
  mMod(prob, Rob, pm, regArch, storeBuf);
  // after
  RegArch  regArch            ///MD  <GROUP>
  {tagMgmt.mpft};             ///HC  <GROUP>   (per-arg domain; tagMgmt/mpft=CTRL_HC)
  mMod(prob, Rob,             ///MD  <GROUP>
    pm, regArch, storeBuf);   ///HC  <GROUP>


=====================================================================
WORDS USED BELOW
=====================================================================
  tag      the comment at the end of a line:  ///CTRL_HC ARF
  domain   is the line about CONTROL or about DATA?
  kind     what the line DOES (MD, HC, HWD, CL, DT, PARAM, HLH)
  target   what the line writes to (usually the left side of "=")
  bundle   one name holding control AND data. It gets two tags joined
           by "+", and each one scores 0.5 instead of 1.0.
  ctor     constructor. In Kathryn its arguments are the wires.




=====================================================================
EXCLUSIONS -- lines we never tag
=====================================================================
  1. COMMENTS. Lines with only //, ///, ///// or a /** ... */ block.
     A code line that merely ENDS with // still gets its tag.

  2. ///DC = "exclude this line". We keep the marker as a record.
       Kathryn : simulation prob -- initProbe, tryInitProbe,
                 dataStructProbGrp.*.init(...)
       Verilog : a copy of something already counted -- see THE
                 10-LINE RULE below; and any feature that BOTH designs
                 switch off ON PURPOSE.

     THE 10-LINE RULE -- what counts as a copy.
     A duplicate is excluded only when the duplicated UNIT is at least
     10 lines long. A short edit or a one-line difference is never
     excluded on its own. The units are:
       - a whole module instance      src_manager srcmng2
       - a whole datapath copy        the second issue path in
                                      pipeline.v
       - a whole extra RS entry       rs_alu_ent ent1..ent7, and the
                                      same in rs_branch / rs_ldst /
                                      rs_mul. Only ent0 is counted,
                                      because Kathryn describes all N
                                      entries with ONE Table/Slot body.

  3. DEAD FILES. If no module in a file is used, MOVE the file to
     fpga/deleted/ Example:
     ram_sync.v (ram_sync_2r2w) is unused; the design uses the version
     without latches. The counting step skips the "deleted" folder
     completely. (///DC removes single lines inside a file still in use.)

  4. STRUCTURE ONLY. #include / `include, namespace X {, include
     guards (#ifndef / #define GUARD / #endif), `timescale, empty
     lines, and lines with only { } }; begin end endmodule endcase
     endgenerate.
     But a `define that defines a CONSTANT is PARAM, not structure.

  5. Host assert(...) and debug code.


=====================================================================
GROUPS  (use the same names on both sides)
=====================================================================
CORE   FETCH   DECODE   DISPATCH
RSV_SHARED   RSV_ALU   RSV_BRANCH   RSV_LDST   RSV_MUL
EXEC_ALU   EXEC_BRANCH   EXEC_LDST   EXEC_MUL
ROB   COMMIT   ARF   RRF   MPFT   TAG   STOREBUF   SHARED_COMP

pipeline.v holds many blocks in one 1935-line file, so give each region
a GROUP using these steps in order.

  1. NEAREST INSTANTIATED SUBMODULE
      pipeline_if pipe_if                        -> FETCH
      tag_generator taggen                       -> TAG
      decoder dec1 / dec2                        -> DECODE
      arf aregfile                               -> ARF
      rrf rregfile + rrf_freelistmanager rrf_fl  -> RRF
      sourceoperand_manager / src_manager / imm_gen /
        brimm_gen / rs_requestgenerator          -> DISPATCH
      rs_alu / rs_ldst / rs_branch / rs_mul +
        alloc_issue_ino                          -> RSV_*
      exunit_alu byakko / suzaku, exunit_ldst seiryu,
        exunit_branch kirin, dmem                -> EXEC_*
      miss_prediction_fix_table mpft             -> MPFT
      reorderbuf rob                             -> ROB / COMMIT

  2. SIGNAL PREFIX, for separate assign / always lines between
     instances
      *_id                                       -> DECODE
      pc* / npc* / inst* / *_if                  -> FETCH
      sptag* / spec* / tagreg* / brdepth         -> TAG
      mpft_*                                     -> MPFT
      adat* / abusy* / *tag / settag*            -> ARF
      rdat* / rvalid* / com*data / *_renamed /
        rrfptr / freenum                         -> RRF
      comptr* / comnum / arfwe* / dp*_addr /
        exfin_* / stcommit                       -> ROB / COMMIT
      *_alu1 / _alu2 / _ldst / _branch / _mul,
        including buf_*                          -> RSV_* / EXEC_*
      sb_* / st* / hitsb / ldaddr / retptr       -> STOREBUF

  3. TIE-BREAK: inside a .port(sig) map use the INSTANCE group, not the
     wire-name group.

